+The public parent-deadline receipt guard marks overall acceptance failed using
+fixed `watchdog_timeout` while retaining measured worker cells and unknown fields.
+It first preserves the original receipt bytes in an invocation-owned private file,
+then binds their digest and original status in the aggregate. Replacement uses an
+exclusive same-directory private temporary file and atomic rename. Absent,
+malformed or invalid-status evidence is not synthesized. Fixed unavailable or
+persistence-failure categories retain the primary timeout without copying command
+or exception bodies. A reserved supervisor-annotation collision fails closed with
+`annotation_conflict`; it does not overwrite the worker's unknown data. An
+unchanged worker status remains provisional because the parent failed. Controls
+cover valid, missing, malformed and failed receipts plus serialization, write,
+fsync and replacement failures. Existing-root refusal remains authoritative.
+These service-free source controls do not recover the missing private inspector
+or specification and do not qualify provider, metadata or native execution.
